1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Hollywood Leading Ladies — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,085
Welcome to Hollywood Leading Ladies, Then and Now.

3
00:00:15,185 --> 00:00:21,853
Julia Roberts became a global favorite with Pretty
Woman, then gave Erin Brockovich a sharp,
determined center.

4
00:00:21,953 --> 00:00:26,630
Across the years, her famous smile still carries
both comedy and conviction.

5
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:31,805
Angelina Jolie has moved between action spectacle,
intimate drama, directing, and humanitarian work.

6
00:00:31,905 --> 00:00:38,573
Lara Croft, Girl Interrupted, and Maleficent show
only a few of the contrasting images in her career.

7
00:00:38,673 --> 00:00:42,554
Nicole Kidman has made reinvention part of her
screen language.

8
00:00:42,654 --> 00:00:51,710
From Moulin Rouge to The Hours, The Others, and Big
Little Lies, she can make glamour, suspense, and
quiet vulnerability feel equally precise.

9
00:00:51,810 --> 00:00:58,180
Compare the early and recent portraits and notice
how each actress has reshaped a familiar image.

10
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,924
The next three leading ladies carry that story
forward.

11
00:01:07,024 --> 00:01:13,581
Kate Winslet made Rose unforgettable in Titanic,
then kept seeking complicated characters in films
and television dramas.

12
00:01:13,681 --> 00:01:17,105
Her work often feels lived in rather than posed.

13
00:01:17,205 --> 00:01:28,069
Charlize Theron has crossed from the dramatic
transformation of Monster to the physical force of
Mad Max Fury Road, proving that range can be both
emotional and athletic.

14
00:01:28,169 --> 00:01:33,552
Anne Hathaway first introduced many viewers to a
shy princess in The Princess Diaries.

15
00:01:33,652 --> 00:01:41,383
Later roles in The Devil Wears Prada, Les
Miserables, and Interstellar revealed a performer
comfortable with wit, music, and depth.

16
00:01:41,483 --> 00:01:43,341
Six portraits, six evolving careers.

17
00:01:43,441 --> 00:01:48,140
Which role appears in your mind the moment you see
each face?

18
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The close-up chapter begins. Look again at the portraits, the years, and the roles.

19
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:31,600
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?

20
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:59,600
